WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.630
If you want to hear how M Night Shyamalan
planted clues about Split and Glass way back

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.540
when he made Unbreakable in the year 2000,
then stick around to the around to the end

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.360
of this video.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.950
Welcome aboard, this special episode of Things
You Missed.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.160
And yes, I already know what you’re thinking.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.070
No CZ, you can’t cover Unbreakable.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.450
It’s not a horror movie.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.450
OK, hold on.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.850
Don’t tell me the scene at the Usmani family’s
house isn’t terrifying.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.700
And second, I’m doing this because I’m
covering the entire series, which includes

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.700
Split.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.700
A horror movie.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.730
And also, I just want to do Unbreakable, and
it’s my channel and I can do what I want.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:01.230
And if you haven’t seen Split, you’ll
want to have seen that as well as Unbreakable.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.140
So with that being said, let’s take a look
at Unbreakable.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.899
The first scene shows the birth of Elijah
Price, and we first see the child who would

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:12.310
later become known as Mr. Glass, through the
reflection of a glass mirror.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.340
This is a common theme in Unbreakable, we’re
introduced to age 13 Elijah through the reflection

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.420
of the Glass television screen, and we’re
introduced to Adult Elijah through the reflection

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.060
of the glass in one of the pieces at his art
gallery.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.450
When David meets Elijah for the first time,
not only are we looking through a glass window,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.670
but the characters are framed in a box, just
like a comic book.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.960
"Here by appointment only."

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.160
"I got a card from this store."

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.000
The reason for these choices is that Elijah
sees himself as nothing more than a fragile,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.149
broken piece of glass, and his entire purpose
throughout the film is to find his real place

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:48.819
in the world, and discover why he is the way
he is.

00:01:48.819 --> 00:01:51.920
In the next scene we’re introduced to the
protagonist, David Dunn.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.759
Note the alliteration of his name like many
other superheroes: Clark Kent, Peter Parker,

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:58.499
Bruce Banner and several others.

00:01:58.499 --> 00:02:02.570
One of the first moments of David being on
screen has him looking at a child in the seat

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.749
in front of him, who is upside-down.

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:08.240
Like the recurrent theme of glass, inversion
is also something that’s seen time and time

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.970
again in Unbreakable, and to understand it,
it’s important to understand the connection

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.280
between the film’s two central characters.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.530
David and Elijah are opposites in every way
but one.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.750
One is invincible, the other of as fragile
as they come.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.720
One gets sick very easily, the other is never
sick.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.040
One is physically gifted, the other has a
hard time even getting around.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.230
David is light skinned, Elijah has dark skin.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.290
David is very reserved, while Elijah is quite
outgoing.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.610
And of course, David is the hero, while Elijah
is the villain.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.580
So when all is right with the world, the camera
is upright, as it should be.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.170
But when disaster is about to strike… when
something bad is about to happen, the camera

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:48.710
is inverted in relation to its subject, the
upside down girl precedes the train crash,

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.830
David’s son Joseph watches TV upside-down
before learning of the crash, Elijah lays

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:56.770
eyes on the comic book that first gives him
the idea that he’s a supposed to be a supervillain

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:00.670
and it’s upside-down, Elijah falls down
the stairs and sees the man with the gun get

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:04.950
away with an inverted perspective and Joseph
sees his dad lift an impossible amount of

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.750
weight from upside-down which later leads
him to pull a gun on his father.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.600
There’s also an inversion reference hidden
in the credits.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.480
David’s wife is named Audrey Dunn, but there’s
a separate credit for the actress who played

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.820
the age 20 Audrey before her and David were
married, where she’s referred to as Audrey

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.820
Inverso.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:24.740
Finally, Elijah discovers a comic that helps
him find out what David’s kryptonite is

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.960
and that’s upside down as well.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.540
Speaking of that kryptonite, that one weakness
that David has, David tells Kelly, the woman

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.790
he meets on the train, that he’s thinking
about getting into male synchronised swimming,

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.850
which is funny because we later find that
his weakness is water.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:42.430
Director M Night Shyamalan also used the idea
of water as a weakness in his next film, Signs.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.920
There’s also a connection to his previous
film, The Sixth Sense, in that Bruce Willis

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.810
is the star of both movies.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:51.810
David’s wife also mentions that her favorite
song is Soft and Wet by the artist formerly

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.740
known as Prince.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.620
Another word for soft is weak, and David becomes
weaker whenever he gets wet.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.560
Kelly also asks David if he likes football,
and he says, “not really”.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.090
We later find out this is a lie, David was
a huge football star, and he still works as

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.200
a security guard at his former school’s
stadium so that he can continue to be around

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.200
the game.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.710
Kelly is going to Philadelphia to meet with
a cornerback from Temple University, who later

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.820
appears in the movie, he’s in the park playing
football with a bunch of kids, one of which

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.130
is David’s son.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.160
One last thing on the train, this isn’t
confirmed, but I’ve got a hunch that this

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.510
could be Kevin Wendell Crumb’s father, who
is said to have disappeared on a train when

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.000
Kevin was young and never come back.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.100
"But you've never met The Beast.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.660
Because he doesn't reside with the rest of
you.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:39.550
Because he resides in the trainyard, as the
story goes, because Kevin's dad left on a

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.550
train.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:46.120
But the fact is: you and Patricia have never
met The Beast."

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.460
Alright, looks like this is my stop.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.300
Alright, always good to be back.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.540
So where were we?

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.020
After the accident, Joseph is seen watching
television.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:12.520
"I don't know how close they're going to be
able to get David, there are woods and trees.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.460
It's going to be a very difficult rescue.."

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.540
It starts with this Dole commercial featuring
a skateboarding Banana, then he flips the

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.950
channel to Jerry Springer, then the Powerpuff
Girls, which is a 90s superhero cartoon, and

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:34.290
then an episode of I Am Weasel, another 90s
cartoon, this episode is about a smart banana

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.960
that comes to life, it’s actually a really
funny episode.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.500
I’m not entirely sure why there are two
separate references to a living, sentient

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.210
banana, perhaps an early foreshadowing of
The Horde, whose defining color is yellow.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.860
Or maybe something with Banana Split?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.160
Could be something there.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.930
I should also probably explain the color scheme
for anyone who hasn’t seen my Glass trailer

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:54.930
analysis.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:59.190
David is almost always wearing Green, from
his shirt in scene two to his iconic rain

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.190
poncho.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.730
Elijah can mostly be found wearing purple
and the present from his mother is wrapped

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.730
in purple.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.470
It even goes right down to Elijah’s purple
walled office and David’s kitchen with the

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.760
green cabinets, which looks beautiful when
complimented by the orange accents after David

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:16.710
defeats the Orange man… oh man we could
talk about color theory all day with this

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.190
movie, but let’s switch back to wherever
we were.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.190
Right.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.190
The TV.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.620
The news of the train wreck comes in on channel
4 news, whose logo resembles the logo of the

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.169
Marvel superhero group, the Fantastic Four.

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:32.199
So David ends up being the only survivor of
the train crash, and after the memorial, receives

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:37.060
a note from Elijah, which leads him to discover
he’s never actually been sick.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.650
Then we get the previously mentioned flashback
to Elijah’s childhood where he receives

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:44.560
the gift from his mother, a comic book titled
The Battle With Jaguaro.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:49.250
Jaguaro is a beast like antagonist wearing
yellow and a reference to The Beast from Split.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:53.470
Jaguaro is going up against a superhero wearing
green, obviously a reference to David.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.120
“They say this one has a surprise ending.”

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.949
Yes, it does.

00:06:58.949 --> 00:07:03.190
Elijah tries to sell the original artwork
as an adult, calling it a classic depiction

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.600
of good vs. evil.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:08.460
However, when he learns that the buyer wants
to get this as a present for his kid, Elijah

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.669
is outraged.

00:07:09.669 --> 00:07:13.190
And I love that little moment where Elijah
is explaining that this is an art gallery,

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:17.120
not a toy store, and he asks the prospective
buyer, do you see any Teletubbies in here?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.180
And the guy actually looks, like “oh my
God, there’s no teletubbies in here!”

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:25.120
But anyway, after David meets Elijah, and
thinks he’s a scam artist, which is interesting

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.260
in itself considering David’s innate ability
to sense evil, David goes home and reads the

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.510
newspaper article about the train crash of
Eastrail 177.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:36.600
The photo of the wreck is credited to Kevin
Ladson, and he's actually the prop master

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.900
of the movie.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.030
In the article, the name of the transportation
secretary is Kia Dickerson, who is also on

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.270
the art department of Unbreakable.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.770
Part of the article mentions that the trains
had just had an engine check prior to leaving

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.040
the station, an early hint that foul play
was involved.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.699
On the right column, there’s an article
about raising money to build prisons

00:07:52.699 --> 00:07:54.190
FOR YOU AND ME TO LIVE IN

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:58.490
Excuse me, to house the number of inmates
expected in the next decade, perhaps some

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.740
of the criminals caught by David Dunn will
inhabit these prisons.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.400
Then David takes a look back at the newspaper
highlights from his football career.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.449
One of the articles is written by Scott Murphy,
Shyamalan’s assistant art director, and

00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:13.610
the photographer Jim Feng is a reference to
James Feng, another assistant art director.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.240
Here’s another reason I love this movie,
always good to see the Brewers losing.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:21.350
The article about David’s car crash in college
is written by Robert Holtzman, yet another

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.600
assistant set decorator.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.560
He’s interrupted from reliving his glory
days when his wife comes knocking on his door

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.050
asking if David has been with anyone since
they started having problems.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:32.360
“I’m prepared for any answer.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.060
It won’t affect me.”

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:35.060
She’s lying.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:36.440
“The answer won’t affect me.”

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.440
She’s lying.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.400
"It won’t affect me either way.”

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.620
She’s lying.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.560
“No.”

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.100
Told you.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.170
The next day at work, Elijah shows up and
we’re introduced to David’s ability to

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:53.860
sense bad people in a crowd, when he predicts
that a man wearing camouflage is carrying

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.060
a silver weapon with a black grip and that
he will step out of line, which he does.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.430
Elijah sets out to see if David’s prediction
is correct.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.600
He steps out of his car which is completely
covered in padding, in order to pursue the

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:07.420
guy, but on the stairs to the subway, has
a bad fall, and the shattering of his glass

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.210
cane represents his frailty.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.570
I already talked about these scenes, so let’s
move onto the next stadium scene.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.270
A single mother in red bumps into him and
he heads the sounds of child abuse.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:20.160
Roll it like the spirit of Philadelphia.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.560
“No….”

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:31.560
Maybe… just maybe… this kid is a young
Kevin Wendell Crumb from Split, but it might

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:32.860
be impossible to know for sure.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:38.070
It is a different actress playing the Mom,
but is has been 15 years so it's just possible

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:42.029
that they weren't able to get that woman who
was an extra on set back to play the Mom.

00:09:42.029 --> 00:09:43.029
I don't know.

00:09:43.029 --> 00:09:44.470
Let me know what your thoughts on that are
in the comments though.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.580
Then there’s a cameo from the director M
Night Shyamalan himself.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.980
David is called away from work because his
son Joseph has an injury at school, when he

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:55.290
gets in a fight with two kids, who we later
find out are Potter and some other guy.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:59.220
“It was Potter and another guy.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:02.640
They were messing with this Chinese girl
in the dressing room.”

00:10:02.642 --> 00:10:05.720
You may remember Potter is the cousin of the
Cornerback from temple.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.529
“He’s Potter’s cousin.

00:10:07.529 --> 00:10:10.850
He’s starting cornerback at Temple University.”

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.650
Then we’ve got Joseph’s gun scene.

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:17.410
Now supposedly this was inspired by an incident
that really happened to Superman actor George

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:21.320
Reeves, where a child confronted him with
a gun and asked to shoot him to prove Superman

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.700
was invincible, and Reeves convinced him to
put the gun down by telling him that someone

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.120
might be injured by the ricochet.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:30.050
I don’t know if that story is true, but
either way it could have been used as inspiration

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:31.420
for the Unbreakable scene.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:35.090
Finally, David revisits the wrecked train
cars and remembers the incident he and Audrey

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:39.149
went through in college, where we has actually
completely unharmed in the car accident.

00:10:39.149 --> 00:10:42.730
He decides to become a vigilante, and saves
the two girls from the orange man.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:45.980
In the newspaper article that comes out the
next day we find out that those girls were

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.200
tied up like that for 3 days.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:52.110
The author of the article is Nicole Marsella,
of course an Art Department assistant.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:55.930
Scott Murphy, the sportswriter from before
also has something to say about the breaking

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.850
up of farmland in this other article, so this
man has many passions it seems, and the farmland

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:05.180
stuff could be another hint towards Signs
being Shyamalan’s next film.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:22.620
Finally, David visits Elijah’s art gallery
showing and meets his mother.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.450
“See the villains eyes?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.740
They’re larger than the other characters.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:32.490
They insinuate a slightly skewed perspective
of how they see the world.”

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:37.290
These are just a couple final clues towards
the reveal that’s about to happen in a couple

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.290
minutes.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.709
Elijah has always seen the world from a skewed
perspective through those big eyes of his.

00:11:41.709 --> 00:11:44.040
But what’s truly amazing is her next comment.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:47.000
“But he says there’s always two kinds.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:53.290
There’s the soldier villain who fights the
hero with his hands… and then there’s

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:58.860
the real threat, the brilliant and evil arch-enemy…
who fights the hero with his mind.”

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:03.030
Shyamalan was planning to bring The Horde
from Split into the equation from the very

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.030
beginning.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:07.490
In fact, he would later reveal that the horde
was at one point supposed to be a part of

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.780
Unbreakable, but he cut the character and
saved him for Split because the movie was

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.780
getting too crowded.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:16.370
I’ve got one more Thing You Missed, but
first remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.830
new horrors every week.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.860
Next week I’m going to be doing Things You
Missed in Split, and you definitely don’t

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:24.480
want to miss out on that, so make sure your
deathbell notifications are on.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.741
The final freeze frame of the movie states
Elijah Price is in an institution for the

00:12:28.741 --> 00:12:30.269
criminally insane.

00:12:30.269 --> 00:12:34.240
Why would it say that if this is not a true
story, and Shyamalan wasn’t planning on

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:39.720
having Glass take place in that institution
19 years later?

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.820
I’ll see you in the next one.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.040
Assuming we both survive.

